      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rochester was platted in 1890 and named after Rochester, Indiana, the native home of a first settler.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town once thrived as a timber boom town thanks to early railroad lines, then became famous for its strawberries after the industry declined.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.experienceolympia.com/our-communities/rochester/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every June, Rochester hosts Swede Day, a festival celebrating the town’s Swedish heritage with a parade, maypole dance, and traditional cuisine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Swede Hall, a historic building built in a Swedish hall style, received $200,000 in 2019 for infrastructure improvements.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Black River Habitat Management Area, the Glacial Heritage Preserve, and the Scatter Creek Unit surround Rochester, offering natural scenery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
